From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT=1: when the allocator holds over 512 MiB that no census field names, its detailed map is written (at most 3 a session); count only, off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT=1 (exact "1"), EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT_MIB=<MiB> (unset or 0:
512). Needs EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS=1 (it runs inside the census's GPU-thread step). Lines (stderr):
"EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT <n>: the allocator uses ... MiB, ... MiB of it in no census field ..."
then the port's "MKW_VMA_MAP tag=90000<n> bytes=... written=1"; the map is
/data/eglantineps5/logs/mkw-vma-<pid>-90000<n>.json (VMA's detailed JSON: every allocation's kind,
size and usage flags).

Why (READ): the allocator's use less everything the census names (images, decode images, copy
buffers, staging, the buffer cache) is about 190 MiB in steady play (docked n=3..261: 186-262 MiB).
At loads it is larger and drains within 3 s (626, 813, 894 MiB). At the two crash loads of
13 Nov it was 1309 MiB (handheld n=51) and 1132 MiB (docked n=311) and did not drain: the graphics
thread was stuck behind the memory. No log line names it. This writes the allocator's own list at
that moment, on the GPU thread (which owns the allocator), so a decode image (storage use only), a
render target and a texture can be told apart. The map is built on the heap (about 1 KB an
allocation; ~3,100 allocations at the handheld refusal) and not written past 8 MiB
(EdenVmaSnapshot). Off: one test of a static per census answer.

diff --git a/src/video_core/memory_census.h b/src/video_core/memory_census.h
index 67359b450f..698f7a2d1e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/memory_census.h
+++ b/src/video_core/memory_census.h
@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@ extern "C" void eden_guest_memory_report(void) __attribute__((weak));
 // vulkan_memory_allocator.cpp as the port adapts it (EDEN_VMA_USAGE): blocks and use, all heaps.
 extern "C" void eden_vma_usage(unsigned long long* blocks, unsigned long long* used)
     __attribute__((weak));
+// The same file: the allocator's detailed map (every block and allocation, with its kind, size and
+// usage flags) into /data/eglantineps5/logs/mkw-vma-<pid>-<100000 + seconds>.json, and one
+// "MKW_VMA_MAP tag=... bytes=... written=..." line (EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT).
+extern "C" void eden_vma_probe(unsigned seconds) __attribute__((weak));
 // The console's RADV (tools/patch-radv-memory-report.py, as isolate-radv.py names it).
 extern "C" void eden_radv_private_radv_ps5_memory_report_now(void) __attribute__((weak));
 namespace Common {
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
index a17273b97e..aa121fd74b 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.cpp
@@ -3279,6 +3279,58 @@ void TextureCacheRuntime::PublishMemoryCensus() {
     Census::Set(Census::StagingStream, stream);
     Census::Set(Census::VmaBlocks, blocks);
     Census::Set(Census::VmaUsed, used);
+    // EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT=1 (exactly "1"; off: one test of a static). What the allocator
+    // holds that no census field names: its use less the images (CensusTick set them just
+    // before this), the decode images, the copy buffers, the staging buffers and the buffer
+    // cache's last figure. About 190 MiB in steady play on the console; at the loads of
+    // crash-20261113-064906 and -063844 1309 and 1132 MiB, which nothing in the logs names. Past
+    // EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT_MIB (unset: 512), at most 3 times a session, the allocator's
+    // detailed map goes to a file (eden_vma_probe, tag 900000 + n): every allocation with its kind
+    // (image or buffer), size and usage flags, so a decode image (storage only), a render target
+    // and a texture can be told apart. Here, on the GPU thread, which owns the allocator. The map
+    // is built on the heap (about 1 KB an allocation) and is not written past 8 MiB.
+    static const bool snapshot_on = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0';
+    }();
+    if (snapshot_on) [[unlikely]] {
+        static const u64 snapshot_limit = [] {
+            const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT_MIB");
+            const u64 mib = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0ULL;
+            return (mib != 0 ? mib : 512ULL) << 20;
+        }();
+        static u32 snapshots = 0;
+        const auto& values = Census::Get().values;
+        const u64 listed = values[Census::Images].load(std::memory_order_relaxed) + in_flight +
+                           kept + copy + held[0] + held[1] + held[2] + stream +
+                           values[Census::Buffers].load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
+        const u64 unlisted = used > listed ? used - listed : 0;
+        if (unlisted > snapshot_limit && snapshots < 3) {
+            ++snapshots;
+            bool can_map = false;
+#if VIDEO_CORE_CENSUS_FRONT
+            can_map = eden_vma_probe != nullptr;
+#endif
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_UP_AREA_VMA_SNAPSHOT %u: the allocator uses %llu MiB, %llu MiB of "
+                         "it in no census field (images %llu, decode %llu, staging %llu, "
+                         "buffers %llu MiB)%s\n",
+                         snapshots, static_cast<unsigned long long>(used >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(unlisted >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(
+                             values[Census::Images].load(std::memory_order_relaxed) >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>((in_flight + kept) >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>((held[0] + held[1] + held[2] + stream) >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(
+                             values[Census::Buffers].load(std::memory_order_relaxed) >> 20),
+                         can_map ? "; map: the MKW_VMA_MAP line below" : "; no map here");
+#if VIDEO_CORE_CENSUS_FRONT
+            if (can_map) {
+                eden_vma_probe(800000U + snapshots);
+            }
+#endif
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 bool TextureCacheRuntime::CanDownloadMsaa(const VideoCommon::ImageInfo& info) const {
